# Git ownership

Humans and agents share the same files. Git is the store. OKMate does not
replace the repository with a hosted wiki.

## Directory roots

A local folder you own is writable. Author Markdown there, commit with git,
and re-run `okmate check` on that path.

## Git roots

A configured git root is a read-only snapshot. `okmate sync` fetches it into
the cache (`OKMATE_CACHE`, default `~/.okmate/cache`). Do not expect
`check` or `inspect` to write into a remote.

## Secrets

`okmate roots --format json` emits `{ id, kind, path, revision, incoming, enabled, error }`.
It never includes tokens or resolved secrets.

## Settings

Config, cache, and session live under `~/.okmate/` (`OKMATE_CONFIG`,
`OKMATE_CACHE`, `OKMATE_STATE`). Installing or updating the app does not
rewrite those paths.
